{"id":"u-37069f60-2db4-43d0-a4e9-77b5f4cf02dd","src":"community","title":"Samson Protocol","author":"Tyler Vaden","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/cn7B9F-samson-protocol","desc":"The Samson Protocol is a 12-week aesthetic specialization program designed to deliberately expand the upper frame, develop balanced muscular proportion, and build strength with discipline and longevity in mind. The primary focus of this phase is chest dominance, capped side delts, fuller arms, and increased lat width — creating a wider, more structured silhouette while maintaining athletic lower-body balance.\n\nThis program prioritizes intentional hypertrophy over ego lifting. Every training day is structured to maximize visual impact: building an upper chest shelf, increasing medial delt volume for shoulder width, improving biceps peak and arm thickness, and enhancing lat width to create a pronounced V-taper. Lower body training supports posture, strength, and overall symmetry without excessive fatigue that would compromise upper-body development.\n\nSamson is not a powerlifting cycle and not a maximal strength pursuit. Strength is developed as a tool, not as the end goal. The emphasis is controlled progression, intelligent volume, and joint-conscious execution. Exercises are selected and structured to stimulate growth while protecting the elbows, wrists, and shoulders through strategic loading, cable-dominant arm work, and deliberate tempo control.\n\nThis phase also integrates weekly mobility and functional training to improve tissue resilience, shoulder mechanics, hip mobility, and long-term performance sustainability. The objective is not only to build muscle but to reinforce structural integrity so progress can continue for years without breakdown.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle","Women's"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-03-14T12:57:44.890Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Chest + Abs","Lats